00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.210
to answering your questions.

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:49.980
The first question is about the
pros and cons of daily caffeine

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:51.870
consumption.

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:54.870
The question reads, what is
your opinion on the net benefit

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:56.430
of daily caffeine consumption?

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:59.220
And how can somebody determine
if daily caffeine consumption

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:00.790
is right for them?

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:03.840
Well, first of all, I did an
entire episode about caffeine.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:06.030
You can find that by
going to hubermanlab.com.

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:09.720
At that website, you can put
in caffeine into the search

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.790
function, and you'll find
links to that episode

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:12.780
in all the formats--

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:14.490
YouTube, Apple,
Spotify, et cetera.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:15.990
And it's timestamped, of course.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:17.880
You can navigate to
the particular topics

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:19.470
most of interest to you.

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:21.630
However, for sake
of this discussion,

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:24.637
I can summarize a few
of the key points.

00:02:24.637 --> 00:02:26.220
The most important
thing to understand

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.990
is that for most adults--

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:32.490
so that is people about
age 18 to 20 and older--

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:34.860
daily caffeine
consumption is not

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:39.360
going to be a problem provided
it does not induce anxiety,

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:42.570
and certainly provided that
it not induce anxiety or panic

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:45.450
attacks, and provided
that it does not

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:48.150
disrupt your nighttime sleep.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:50.370
This is why I always
recommend that if you

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:54.150
are going to consume caffeine
in any form, coffee, tea, soda,

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:57.900
or otherwise, that you
try not to ingest caffeine

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.600
within the eight and
ideally within the 10

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:03.190
or even 12 hours
prior to bedtime.

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:05.280
That's because the
half life of caffeine

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.613
is such that even
if you are able to,

00:03:07.613 --> 00:03:09.030
for instance, have
a cup of coffee

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:11.370
around 3:00 PM or
4:00 PM and then

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:15.360
fall asleep around midnight,
the architecture of the sleep

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.910
that you get is going
to be disrupted.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:20.160
For instance, it
is very important

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:23.220
that you get sufficient amounts
of both slow wave deep sleep

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:26.020
as well as rapid eye
movement sleep each night.

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:28.830
And if you consume caffeine
too close to bedtime--

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:32.520
and here, I'm defining to close
as anywhere from 8 to 12 hours

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:33.870
before going to sleep--

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:36.900
chances are you're not going to
get as much rapid eye movement

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:40.980
sleep or slow wave sleep
that you would otherwise.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:43.200
And it is the amount of
rapid eye movement sleep

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.420
and slow wave sleep
that, together,

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:47.760
lead to whether or not you
feel you had a good night's

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:51.150
sleep in terms of your next
day alertness and cognitive

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:51.900
abilities.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:53.730
Now, again, some people
may find that they

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:56.430
can drink caffeine in the late
afternoon, maybe even at night,

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:57.390
and still fall asleep.

00:03:57.390 --> 00:04:00.000
But I promise you, even if
you're in that category,

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.138
you will sleep far better,
meaning the architecture

00:04:03.138 --> 00:04:04.680
of your sleep will
be better, and you

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:07.080
will feel far more
rested the next day

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.990
if you abstain from caffeine
within the eight to 12 hours

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:11.400
prior to bedtime.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:14.220
And I should also say that
none of us are perfect,

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.430
myself included.

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:18.375
I will sometimes have a cup of
coffee in the late afternoon,

00:04:18.375 --> 00:04:21.000
and sometimes that will cause me
to stay up a little bit later.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.170
Sometimes it won't.

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:24.300
I don't think you want
to obsess or worry

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.610
too much about having
some caffeine every once

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:28.513
in a while in the
late afternoon if you

00:04:28.513 --> 00:04:30.180
are still able to
fall asleep, but don't

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:31.620
make it a regular habit.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:35.070
Now, as far as we know,
there is no drawback

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:37.320
to consuming caffeine
on a daily basis,

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:40.110
again, provided it does not
disrupt your nighttime sleep

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:43.230
and provided that does
not induce anxiety.

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:45.450
In fact, most of
the world consumes

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:47.220
caffeine every single day.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:50.010
The current estimates
are that 90%--

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:52.860
that's right, 9-0, 90%--

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:56.430
of adults throughout the world
consume a caffeinated beverage

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:58.090
every single day.

00:04:58.090 --> 00:04:59.550
That's a staggeringly
high number,

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:03.190
making caffeine the most
popular drug on the planet.

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:06.198
In fact, because of the
way that caffeine works--

00:05:06.198 --> 00:05:07.740
and just to remind
you how it works--

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.840
it effectively blocks
adenosine receptors.

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:13.420
Adenosine is a molecule
that builds up in your brain

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:17.590
and body more and more according
to how long you've been awake.

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:18.760
It makes you feel sleepy.

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:20.830
Caffeine blocks the
adenosine receptor,

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:24.430
and then when it is dislodged
from that receptor, whatever

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:27.040
adenosine has built up
and is around can then

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:29.200
bind to the adenosine receptor.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.910
It makes you feel very sleepy.

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:32.380
That's the caffeine crash.

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:35.440
So if 90% of the adult
population of the planet Earth

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.060
is consuming caffeine
every day, that

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:40.390
means 90% of the adult
population of planet Earth

00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:42.850
is blocking their
adenosine receptors

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:45.370
for some portion of
their daily life,

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:48.820
and then their adenosine is
binding to the vacant receptor

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:50.980
once the caffeine has dislodged.

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:56.230
And why are 90% of adult humans
consuming caffeine every day?

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:59.020
Well, to feel more
energized, more focused,

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:04.150
to have more both cognitive
energy and physical energy.

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:06.850
Now, of course, most people are
not walking around thinking,

00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:10.090
oh, caffeine gives me more
energy more focus, et cetera.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:13.510
Most people are consuming
caffeine every single day

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:16.210
and are consuming caffeine
every single day in order

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:18.820
to feel, quote,
unquote, normal, to be

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:21.940
at their baseline level
of cognitive ability,

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:24.260
and physical energy, and so on.

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:27.520
In fact, if you look at the data
on caffeine consumption, what

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.740
you'll find is that
caffeine actually

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:31.180
is a cognitive enhancer.

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:32.770
It can improve
learning and memory.

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:34.360
It can increase physical energy.

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:37.180
It can increase mental
and physical stamina.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:40.240
But a feature of those studies
that's not often discussed

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:44.170
but that was, however, discussed
in the full episode on caffeine

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.570
is that studies of
caffeine typically

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:49.240
are done by taking
chronic caffeine users

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:52.720
and then having them abstain
from caffeine for some period

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:56.650
of time, usually four days
to two weeks, in which time

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:58.390
they undergo
caffeine withdrawal.

00:06:58.390 --> 00:06:59.650
They do not feel well.

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.420
They get foggy headed.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:02.990
They have less energy.

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:06.400
There's some malaise, sometimes
even some mild depression.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:08.170
And then what they
do is they have

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:11.860
people take caffeine, and
take a cognitive exam,

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:14.920
or do some physical activity
and compare their performance

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:17.860
to what it was when they
were in the withdrawal state.

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:20.290
Another typical form
of study on caffeine

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:22.630
is to take people who
are naive to caffeine

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:25.420
or who never take caffeine, and
then have them ingest caffeine,

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:28.150
and then measure their cognitive
and/or physical performance.

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:30.080
And in both cases,
you see improvements.

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:33.220
What I'm saying here is that
daily caffeine consumption

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:35.920
is not going to
lead to improvements

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:39.400
in cognitive ability
or improvements

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:41.620
in physical ability
above one's baseline

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:44.230
unless you either
abstain from caffeine

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.540
for some period of time,
typically four days to two

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:49.210
weeks prior, or you
are not somebody

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:51.310
who typically ingests caffeine.

00:07:51.310 --> 00:07:53.950
In other words, 90% of
the world's population

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:56.110
is drinking caffeine
on a daily basis

00:07:56.110 --> 00:07:59.410
to be at their normal level
of mental and physical

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:00.410
functioning.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:02.920
So the question was,
is there a net benefit

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:04.670
to daily caffeine consumption?

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:07.390
And here I can
reliably say, provided

00:08:07.390 --> 00:08:09.670
you don't suffer from anxiety
attacks or lack of sleep

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:11.795
from the caffeine consumption,
provided that you're

00:08:11.795 --> 00:08:14.860
mindful of not ingesting
caffeine too late in the day,

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:18.310
there doesn't seem to be any big
drawback to drinking caffeine

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:19.850
on a daily basis.

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:22.750
However, there doesn't seem
to be any great benefit,

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:25.120
at least in terms
of direct effects

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:27.730
on cognitive or
physical ability.

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:30.980
So I realize this is a little
bit of a convoluted answer,

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:34.059
but we have to be honest
with one another here.

00:08:34.059 --> 00:08:36.820
Caffeine is a
performance-enhancing drug,

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:39.730
but only when compared to
the noncaffeinated state.

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:43.780
And 90% of the adult population
of the world is caffeinated.

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:47.230
So adding more caffeine above
what you would normally consume

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:50.080
is certainly not going to allow
you to think better and perform

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:50.980
better physically.

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:53.110
Here's a useful way to
think about caffeine.

00:08:53.110 --> 00:08:56.350
Most people can pretty well
tolerate doses of caffeine,

00:08:56.350 --> 00:08:59.638
anywhere from 100 milligrams
to 300 milligrams.

00:08:59.638 --> 00:09:01.180
It depends on body
weight and depends

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:03.310
on your tolerance,
tolerance, of course,

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:07.120
based on how familiar you are
with the effects of caffeine

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:08.950
and how regularly
you consume it.

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:11.493
A typical cup of coffee, which,
by the way, does not exist.

00:09:11.493 --> 00:09:12.910
Depending on the
vendor, depending

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:15.430
on how much water-to-coffee
ratio one uses,

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:18.520
depending on whether or not it's
French press or it's pour over,

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:20.350
the type of coffee,
et cetera, all of that

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:23.080
is going to determine the
total amount of caffeine

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:24.320
in that coffee.

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:27.437
But we can set some outer bounds
on the total amount of caffeine

00:09:27.437 --> 00:09:29.020
that likely exists
in a cup of coffee,

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:31.690
and it's probably somewhere
between 100 milligrams--

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:34.660
that would be on the weaker side
for a six or eight ounce cup

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:35.290
of coffee--

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:38.020
out to about 300 milligrams
for the equivalent

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:39.740
six to eight ounces of coffee.

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:42.180
But if you were to brew your
coffee very, very strong

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:44.680
or, like me, occasionally throw
a shot of espresso in there,

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:46.055
too, you could
get that number up

00:09:46.055 --> 00:09:47.920
to 400 or 500
milligrams of caffeine.

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:49.840
I personally tolerate
caffeine pretty well.

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:52.257
I've been drinking caffeine
since I was a teenager, mostly

00:09:52.257 --> 00:09:55.297
in the form of brewed
unflavored yerba mate tea.

00:09:55.297 --> 00:09:57.880
It's important to stay away from
the smoked varieties of yerba

00:09:57.880 --> 00:10:00.505
mate if you're going to get your
caffeine from your yerba mate.

00:10:00.505 --> 00:10:02.800
The smoked varieties
can be carcinogenic.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:07.190
The nonsmoked varieties don't
seem to have that property.

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:09.570
But there's a lot of
caffeine in yerba mate,

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:12.000
so I'll drink yerba mate and
have for many, many years.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.980
Or I'll drink black coffee,
or espresso, or espresso

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:16.320
americano, things of that sort.

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:18.360
That's my preferred
source of caffeine.

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:20.820
Most people are drinking
coffee to get their caffeine

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:22.590
and, I would say
that, if you are

00:10:22.590 --> 00:10:24.210
going to drink your
caffeine, drink it

00:10:24.210 --> 00:10:26.470
in the early part of the
day, as I mentioned earlier.

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:29.100
I am a big proponent of
delaying your first caffeine

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:31.920
intake until at least 90
minutes after waking in order

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:33.177
to avoid the afternoon crash.

00:10:33.177 --> 00:10:35.010
I've talked a lot about
this on the podcast.

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:37.135
There are a lot of clips
on the internet explaining

00:10:37.135 --> 00:10:38.260
the rationale behind that.

00:10:38.260 --> 00:10:40.980
And if you do experience an
afternoon crash in energy,

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:44.190
I do recommend delaying your
morning caffeine intake to 90

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:46.320
to 120 minutes after waking.

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:48.270
Now, for people that
want to get more

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:52.140
of a true cognitive-enhancing
and performance-enhancing

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:53.640
effect from caffeine,
again, you're

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:57.720
going to have to abstain from
caffeine for about four days.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:01.170
For regular caffeine drinkers,
that's going to be difficult.

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:03.293
That is going to
lead to headaches.

00:11:03.293 --> 00:11:04.710
That's going to
lead to brain fog.

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:07.200
That's going to lead
to feelings of malaise.

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:09.840
In fact, the last time
I took four days off

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:12.150
or even a week off from
caffeine consumption

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:13.570
was when I was sick.

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:15.570
I don't get sick very
often, but when I am sick,

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:17.250
I generally abstain
from caffeine.

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:18.792
And sometimes I
wonder whether or not

00:11:18.792 --> 00:11:22.698
the malaise I feel from whatever
viral or bacterial thing

00:11:22.698 --> 00:11:24.240
I might be dealing
with when I'm sick

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.840
is, in part, the malaise
of caffeine withdrawal.

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:28.590
I certainly notice I
feel much better when

00:11:28.590 --> 00:11:30.215
I return to drinking
caffeine, but that

00:11:30.215 --> 00:11:32.428
tends to coincide
with feeling relief

00:11:32.428 --> 00:11:34.470
from whatever sinus symptoms
and other symptoms I

00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:36.130
might have been experiencing
from the illness.

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:37.570
So it's not a good experiment.

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:39.280
I can't tease apart
those variables.

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:40.950
So the short answer
is, for most adults,

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:43.540
there does not seem to be any
major downside to consuming

00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:44.040
caffeine.

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:46.740
And there have been scattered
reports here and there

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:51.000
in humans, showing that
ingesting caffeine can increase

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:54.060
dopamine receptors,
which will effectively

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:57.840
allow you to get more out of
the dopamine that you produce.

00:11:57.840 --> 00:12:00.960
This is why caffeine has
a mood elevating as well

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:02.520
as energy-elevating effect.

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:04.900
I should point out that some
people just cannot tolerate

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:05.400
caffeine.

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:06.930
It makes them too
jittery, too anxious.

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:07.810
They start sweating.

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:09.390
They get heart palpitations.

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:11.700
It's very hard for these
people to build up a tolerance

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:13.408
to caffeine that allows
them to enjoy it.

00:12:13.408 --> 00:12:15.150
These are the
people that can even

00:12:15.150 --> 00:12:17.610
feel a fluttering of the
heart and a lot of energy

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:20.340
left from decaf
coffee, something

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:21.990
that, to me, is just a foreign.

00:12:21.990 --> 00:12:26.020
Concept but some people are
just that sensitive to caffeine

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:28.770
that even the small amounts of
caffeine in chocolate or decaf

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:31.080
coffee make them feel too alert.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:32.760
And they should
abstain from caffeine.

00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:34.740
I don't think they
are, in any way,

00:12:34.740 --> 00:12:37.170
harming their health by
abstaining from caffeine.

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:39.840
Then there's the issue of
children, and adolescents,

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:43.440
and teenagers, and young
adults ingesting caffeine.

00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:46.500
And I covered some of this in
the episode about caffeine,

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:48.870
but there's been a
lot of debate as to

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:51.150
whether or not caffeine
can cause osteoporosis,

00:12:51.150 --> 00:12:53.358
whether or not it can leach
calcium out of the bones,

00:12:53.358 --> 00:12:54.930
whether or not can stunt growth.

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:57.120
Frankly, there's not
a lot of evidence

00:12:57.120 --> 00:13:00.390
for those sorts of claims,
and yet the developing brain

00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:03.240
is a very tender and
malleable environment.

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:05.640
And somebody who
started off his career

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:07.080
as a developmental
neurobiologist,

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:09.870
studying developmental
brain plasticity and wiring,

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:13.350
it does sort of make me cringe
to think about children younger

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:15.960
than the age of,
say, 14 ingesting

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:19.330
large amounts of caffeine in
any form-- soda, coffee, tea, et

00:13:19.330 --> 00:13:19.830
cetera.

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:21.930
Despite the fact that
there's very little evidence

00:13:21.930 --> 00:13:25.080
that it can stunt their
growth, I don't personally

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:27.420
like the idea of the
young brain being bathed

00:13:27.420 --> 00:13:30.240
in an adenosine receptor
antagonist, which is

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:32.220
effectively what caffeine is.

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:35.100
As much as possible, one
wants the developing brain

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:40.020
to develop in a milieu of
unencumbered, nonchemically

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:42.300
encumbered interactions
between neurotransmitters

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:43.950
and their receptors,
unless, of course,

00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:47.220
there's a clinical need
for a prescription drug,

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:50.640
or a supplement, or
some modification

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:52.770
of a nutritional
program specifically

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:55.227
to up or down regulate
the dopamine system

00:13:55.227 --> 00:13:57.060
or up or down regulate
the serotonin system.

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:58.560
But those are the
sorts of decisions

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:01.560
that really should be
made in close oversight

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:04.440
and recommendations
by a psychiatrist.

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:08.670
So the short answer around
daily caffeine consumption

00:14:08.670 --> 00:14:10.890
in young people,
meaning 14 and younger,

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:12.930
is avoid it if you can.

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:15.120
Have your children avoid
caffeine if they can.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:18.023
The occasional bit of
caffeine is probably not

00:14:18.023 --> 00:14:18.940
going to be a problem.

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:21.720
The amount of caffeine in small
amounts of chocolate, probably

00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:22.980
not going to be a problem.

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:26.250
But caffeine in the form of
energy drinks, sodas, coffee,

00:14:26.250 --> 00:14:27.990
tea for children
younger than 14 just

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:29.670
seems like a bad
idea from everything

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:33.120
we understand about brain wiring
and the trajectories of brains

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:35.430
that develop with a lot
of chemical adjustment

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:38.530
from other sources,
like caffeine.

00:14:38.530 --> 00:14:43.890
Now, for kids age 15 to, say,
18 or 20, a lot of brain wiring

00:14:43.890 --> 00:14:46.660
is still occurring, but a
lot of it has been completed.

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:50.610
So probably not as risky
to consume caffeine

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:52.990
every once in a while or
maybe even on a daily basis.

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:53.460
But there are two--

00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:54.877
I think there are
great advantages

00:14:54.877 --> 00:14:57.330
to limiting the amount of
caffeine that one ingests.

00:14:57.330 --> 00:15:00.420
And of course, in the
adolescent and teen years,

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:01.920
nowadays a lot of
kids are consuming

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:03.420
energy drinks and soda.

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:05.100
And some of those
energy drinks and so

00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:06.900
does contain a lot
of caffeine, anywhere

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:09.550
from 200 to 800
milligrams of caffeine.

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:11.800
And nowadays, more
sodas and energy drinks

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:14.560
contain other things like
amino acid precursors

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:16.160
to neuromodulators,
like dopamine.

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:17.830
So for instance, a
lot of energy drinks

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:21.760
now contain L-tyrosine, which
is a precursor to dopamine.

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:23.980
A lot of them will
contain L-theanine.

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:26.230
I've talked about L-theanine
as a supplement that

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:28.570
can promote more
restful sleep if taken

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:30.340
30 to 60 minutes before sleep.

00:15:30.340 --> 00:15:34.660
The reason why a lot of
energy drinks, and sodas,

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:37.660
and, frankly, now coffee
brands are including theanine

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:40.270
in the coffee, or
energy drink, or soda

00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:45.700
is because it tends to have a
mild anxiety-reducing effect.

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:48.590
And it reduces the jitters
that caffeine creates.

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:51.640
And so that's actually a trick
that these companies are using

00:15:51.640 --> 00:15:54.220
in order to get people to
ingest more caffeine because,

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:57.520
by including the theanine, it's
preventing the kid or adult

00:15:57.520 --> 00:15:58.870
from feeling too jittery.

00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:01.540
And therefore, they can
continue to consume that drink

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:03.770
without feeling like
they're overstimulated.

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:09.970
So if I were to take the
parental neuroscientist adult

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:12.970
voice here, I would say
avoid caffeine intake

00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:15.760
as much as you can until
you're about 18 years old.

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:16.540
But I'm realistic.

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:19.780
I realize that adolescents
and teens age, say,

00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:23.020
14, or 15, out to
18, and older are

00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:25.480
going to be consuming caffeine
in the form of energy drinks

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:26.170
and sodas.

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:28.750
But reducing the total
amount of caffeine

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:30.670
that one is ingesting
in those years,

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:32.170
it just seems
really advantageous,

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:34.450
again, m all the same
reasons I mentioned earlier.

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:36.130
You don't want the
young brain bathing

00:16:36.130 --> 00:16:39.280
in a bunch of exogenous,
meaning externally introduced

00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:43.420
neurochemicals or in things
like theanine or L-tyrosine.

00:16:43.420 --> 00:16:47.320
If you're going to indulge
in caffeine, or in energy

00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:50.900
drinks, or theanine, or
L-tyrosine, for that matter,

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:53.260
that's the sort of thing
that probably is best left

00:16:53.260 --> 00:16:54.880
for people 18 and older.

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:57.430
And even there, if one finds
that caffeine is for them,

00:16:57.430 --> 00:17:01.330
as do I, I think always best
to try and get your caffeine

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:03.280
from a clean source,
a clean source meaning

00:17:03.280 --> 00:17:06.640
something that contains
just coffee or just tea.

00:17:06.640 --> 00:17:09.550
Again, this isn't a knock on
energy drink specifically,

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:11.950
but you really have to make
sure that whatever energy

00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:14.829
drink you're going to consume,
you know what's in it.

00:17:14.829 --> 00:17:17.560
You recognize what the
different ingredients do.

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:20.500
And you recognize the
potential of ingesting

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:22.630
those ingredients chronically
over and over again.

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:24.069
And I've talked to a
little bit about this

00:17:24.069 --> 00:17:25.944
on previous podcasts,
and I'll get into this.

00:17:25.944 --> 00:17:29.020
Again, maybe we'll do an entire
episode about energy drinks

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:32.070
because they are so
commonly consumed nowadays.

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:33.820
Now, getting back to
the original question

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:35.470
about daily caffeine
consumption,

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:38.590
this person goes on to
say that, for them--

00:17:38.590 --> 00:17:40.390
OK, this is their
personal experience--

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:43.720
after a few weeks of
consumption of daily caffeine,

00:17:43.720 --> 00:17:45.820
the negatives start to
outweigh the positive ones.

00:17:45.820 --> 00:17:47.278
They're getting
poor-quality sleep,

00:17:47.278 --> 00:17:49.150
lack of appetite,
anxiety, et cetera.

00:17:49.150 --> 00:17:50.830
And when they don't
consume caffeine,

00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:52.615
they find it a lot
easier to be mindful,

00:17:52.615 --> 00:17:54.490
and their meditation
practice is much better.

00:17:54.490 --> 00:17:56.608
But they're lethargic
and less motivated.

00:17:56.608 --> 00:17:58.900
So what they're describing
are all the classic symptoms

00:17:58.900 --> 00:18:02.090
of caffeine overuse, probably
not abuse in this case,

00:18:02.090 --> 00:18:04.090
although caffeine
can be truly abused,

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:08.142
people taking caffeine pills,
et cetera in large quantities.

00:18:08.142 --> 00:18:09.350
We're not talking about that.

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:11.890
But this person is describing
the classic pattern

00:18:11.890 --> 00:18:15.815
of overuse of caffeine and the
classic pattern of withdrawal

00:18:15.815 --> 00:18:17.440
from caffeine when
they stop taking it.

00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:19.763
So what should
somebody like this do?

00:18:19.763 --> 00:18:21.430
And I think that's
an important question

00:18:21.430 --> 00:18:22.690
to answer because I
think a lot of people

00:18:22.690 --> 00:18:23.690
fall into this category.

00:18:23.690 --> 00:18:26.260
They drink caffeine every day.

00:18:26.260 --> 00:18:28.810
They're no longer getting the
performance-enhancing effect

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:30.393
of caffeine, so
they're taking it just

00:18:30.393 --> 00:18:33.070
to be normal or feel like they
can focus normally and have

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:34.370
normal amounts of energy.

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:36.850
But then if they try and
come off, they feel worse.

00:18:36.850 --> 00:18:38.433
There are a couple
of ways to do this.

00:18:38.433 --> 00:18:40.810
You can taper your
caffeine intake off

00:18:40.810 --> 00:18:42.942
over the course of
four to seven days.

00:18:42.942 --> 00:18:44.650
But most people don't
have the discipline

00:18:44.650 --> 00:18:46.520
or don't want to spend
the time doing that.

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:48.687
But if you want to, the way
you would do that is you

00:18:48.687 --> 00:18:51.652
would cut it by about
10% or 15% per day.

00:18:51.652 --> 00:18:53.110
You could do that
by volume, or you

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:56.020
could do that by concentration
of coffee, that sort of thing.

00:18:56.020 --> 00:18:58.773
A simpler way to go about all
this that still will allow

00:18:58.773 --> 00:19:00.940
you to get some of the
performance-enhancing effects

00:19:00.940 --> 00:19:04.270
of caffeine and yet
experience far less withdrawal

00:19:04.270 --> 00:19:05.930
would be two things.

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:08.590
First of all, just
halve your amount

00:19:08.590 --> 00:19:11.853
of caffeine intake
for two or three days.

00:19:11.853 --> 00:19:13.270
So again, that
could be by volume,

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:16.300
or it could be by
concentration, probably easiest

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:17.052
to do by volume.

00:19:17.052 --> 00:19:18.760
And so instead of
drinking an eight ounce

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:20.718
coffee in the morning,
maybe you do four ounces

00:19:20.718 --> 00:19:22.728
of regular coffee,
four ounces of decaf,

00:19:22.728 --> 00:19:24.520
or you just have the
four ounces of coffee.

00:19:24.520 --> 00:19:27.490
You do that for
three or four days,

00:19:27.490 --> 00:19:32.140
and then you take perhaps one
full day off from caffeine,

00:19:32.140 --> 00:19:33.910
maybe another full day off.

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:37.450
You're going to feel a
lot less bad on those

00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:39.790
two days, having cut your
caffeine intake in half

00:19:39.790 --> 00:19:41.457
in the previous four
days then you would

00:19:41.457 --> 00:19:42.910
if you just went cold turkey.

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:45.670
And then you go back
to ingesting caffeine,

00:19:45.670 --> 00:19:49.570
but you go back to ingesting
caffeine at that 50% dose

00:19:49.570 --> 00:19:52.840
or what used to represent that
50% dose of caffeine for you.

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:55.120
And you just continue
that way on a daily basis,

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:56.320
and then every once
in a while, when

00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:58.070
you want the
performance-enhancing effects

00:19:58.070 --> 00:20:01.240
of caffeine, you go back to what
was your original dose, which

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:04.265
is now double what you're
taking on a daily basis.

00:20:04.265 --> 00:20:05.890
So what we're really
talking about here

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:07.000
is not going cold turkey.

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:09.783
We're not talking about
quitting caffeine indefinitely.

00:20:09.783 --> 00:20:12.200
What we're talking about is
cutting the amount of caffeine

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:17.480
that you drink in half for about
four days, plus or minus a day,

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:21.500
and then taking two days off
from caffeine completely.

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:25.980
And then going back on that half
dose of caffeine indefinitely.

00:20:25.980 --> 00:20:28.257
That's your new baseline
of caffeine intake.

00:20:28.257 --> 00:20:29.840
And then every once
in a while, if you

00:20:29.840 --> 00:20:32.660
need a bit more of a lift, you
ingest twice as much caffeine

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:34.595
or a coffee that's
twice as concentrated.

00:20:34.595 --> 00:20:36.470
We should acknowledge
that most people aren't

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:39.800
going to be really precise
about the amount of ounces

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:41.090
and the amount of caffeine.

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:42.787
Nonetheless, it's
pretty straightforward

00:20:42.787 --> 00:20:44.870
to know that you're reducing
your caffeine intake.

00:20:44.870 --> 00:20:46.495
Certainly, it's clear
to know if you're

00:20:46.495 --> 00:20:48.540
ingesting no caffeine
for a couple of days.

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:50.662
And it's pretty clear
when you're doubling

00:20:50.662 --> 00:20:51.620
the amount of caffeine.

00:20:51.620 --> 00:20:53.630
But you don't have to worry
so much that you're exactly

00:20:53.630 --> 00:20:54.860
doubling the amount of caffeine.

00:20:54.860 --> 00:20:56.277
You can drink one
and a half times

00:20:56.277 --> 00:20:58.400
as much as you happen to
drink on the day before,

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:00.827
or you could drink
three times as much.

00:21:00.827 --> 00:21:03.410
You would definitely feel it if
you drink three times as much.

00:21:03.410 --> 00:21:05.120
One very important
thing to recognize

00:21:05.120 --> 00:21:07.970
is that, on any day where you
really spike your caffeine

00:21:07.970 --> 00:21:11.030
intake above baseline, no
matter where that baseline is

00:21:11.030 --> 00:21:12.380
when you start-- it could be 0.

00:21:12.380 --> 00:21:13.940
It could be 400 milligrams.

00:21:13.940 --> 00:21:15.170
It could be 200 milligrams.

00:21:15.170 --> 00:21:20.030
When you double that intake, you
will get a big boost of energy,

00:21:20.030 --> 00:21:23.270
and the next day, you're going
to feel the crash from that.

00:21:23.270 --> 00:21:24.770
You're going to
feel more lethargic.

00:21:24.770 --> 00:21:25.760
You're going to
feel not so good.

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:28.040
This has to do with dopamine
receptor modulation.

00:21:28.040 --> 00:21:30.650
This has to do with adenosine
receptor modulation.

00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:32.358
The important thing
to do is not continue

00:21:32.358 --> 00:21:34.400
to consume that elevated
level of caffeine, which

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:37.100
is what most people do, and then
they set a new hire baseline

00:21:37.100 --> 00:21:38.070
just to feel normal.

00:21:38.070 --> 00:21:43.483
The key thing is to just manage
to get through that crash day,

00:21:43.483 --> 00:21:44.900
manage to get
through that one day

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:47.540
where you feel a little less
good or maybe even down a bit.

00:21:47.540 --> 00:21:48.450
Get outside a bit.

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:49.408
Get some more sunshine.

00:21:49.408 --> 00:21:51.740
We know that spikes your
cortisol in a good way.

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:54.510
It can increase the
catecholamines, dopamine, et

00:21:54.510 --> 00:21:55.010
cetera.

00:21:55.010 --> 00:21:56.240
Get a little bit more sunlight.

00:21:56.240 --> 00:21:57.532
Get a little bit more movement.

00:21:57.532 --> 00:21:58.130
Get outside.

00:21:58.130 --> 00:22:00.172
Do something to offset
those feelings of malaise,

00:22:00.172 --> 00:22:02.540
and then get right back
to your original goal

00:22:02.540 --> 00:22:04.160
level of caffeine each day.

00:22:04.160 --> 00:22:06.980
There's no use in getting so
quantitative that you make

00:22:06.980 --> 00:22:09.020
your life miserable,
you're measuring things out

00:22:09.020 --> 00:22:10.335
like a laboratory chemist.

00:22:10.335 --> 00:22:12.710
If you're that type and you
want to do that, be my guest.

00:22:12.710 --> 00:22:14.668
But unless you're taking
caffeine in pill form,

00:22:14.668 --> 00:22:18.320
it's very, very hard
to get extremely exact

00:22:18.320 --> 00:22:20.580
about the amounts of caffeine
that you're ingesting.

00:22:20.580 --> 00:22:23.600
So it is OK to eyeball it,
but understand the contour

00:22:23.600 --> 00:22:25.730
of how caffeine works
and what the caffeine

00:22:25.730 --> 00:22:27.600
performance-enhancing
effect comes from.

00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:30.020
It comes from a caffeine
intake above baseline.

00:22:30.020 --> 00:22:31.970
Understand that any time
you go above baseline

00:22:31.970 --> 00:22:33.390
with your caffeine
intake, there's

00:22:33.390 --> 00:22:34.760
the potential of some anxiety.

00:22:34.760 --> 00:22:37.670
Understand that there's going
to be a slight withdrawal

00:22:37.670 --> 00:22:41.060
effect that lasts
about 24 to 48 hours.

00:22:41.060 --> 00:22:42.740
Battle through
that short period,

00:22:42.740 --> 00:22:45.050
and you'll be right
back where you started

00:22:45.050 --> 00:22:47.390
and where you need to be so
that you can enjoy caffeine

00:22:47.390 --> 00:22:51.140
on a daily basis and derive
the benefits because there are

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:54.020
many benefits to drinking
caffeine and avoiding

00:22:54.020 --> 00:22:55.340
some of the potential hazards.

00:22:55.340 --> 00:22:57.170
And again, if you're
a young person,

00:22:57.170 --> 00:23:00.320
I recommend delaying that
caffeine intake maybe, I

00:23:00.320 --> 00:23:01.605
don't know, 10 years.

